41949,"d":434},{"n":"BNC Victoire","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":-22.274638,"lo":166.444491,"d":496,"h":"Mo-Fr 08:00-16:00"},{"n":"La Vie Claire","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":-22.268779,"lo":166.441722,"d":501,"h":"Mo 14:00-18:00; Tu 08:00-18:00; We 08:00-18:00; Th 08:00-18:00; Fr 08:00-18:00; Sa 08:00-12:00,14:00-17:30","w":"https://www.lavieclaire.com/magasin-bio/noumea-nouvelle-caledonie.html","ph":"+687 282 001"},{"n":"Nouméa Cathedral","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-22.272778,"lo":166.444444,"d":457,"ds":"Nouméa Cathedral (French: Cathédrale Saint-Joseph de Nouméa) is a Catholic church in Nouméa, New Caledonia. It is dedicated to the Saint Joseph. The cathedral has been the seat since 1966 of the Archdiocese of Nouméa, to which the former Vicariate Apostolic of Nouvelle-Calédonie was elevated.","wpu":"Nouméa Cathedral","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Noum%C3%A9aDom.jpg/960px-Noum%C3%A9aDom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Naval Base Noumea","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-22.270002,"lo":166.419119,"d":2174,"ds":"Naval Base Noumea was a major United States Navy sea and air base at Nouméa, New Caledonia. Naval Base Noumea was built at Noumea Harbor. Noumea was picked for a naval base as it was beyond the range of Japanese land-based planes.","wpu":"Naval Base Noumea","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/NBNoumea_NewCaledonia1942.jpg/960px-NBNoumea_NewCaledonia1942.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Boulari Bay","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-22.253889,"lo":166.526111,"d":9112,"ds":"Boulari Bay or Baie de Boulari is a bay in southwestern New Caledonia. It forms the stretch of water to the east of Noumea.","wpu":"Boulari Bay","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Boulari_Bay.png/960px-Boulari_Bay.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Nouméa (/nuːˈmeɪ.ə/ noo-MAY-uh, nyoo-, -⁠MEE-; French: [numea] ) is the capital and largest city of the French special collectivity of New Caledonia. It is the largest Francophone city in Oceania. It is situated on a peninsula in the south of New Caledonia's main island, Grande Terre, and is home to the majority of the island's European, Polynesian (Wallisians, Futunians, Tahitians), Indonesian, and Vietnamese populations, as well as many Melanesians, Ni-Vanuatu and indigenous Kanaks who work in one of the South Pacific's most industrialised cities.","wpu":"Nouméa","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/View_over_Noumea.jpg/960px-View_over_Noumea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}